    "max_awards": null,
    "plot": "Vex awakens in the Dusty Entryway of the Alchemist's Folly, an underground complex built by the obsessed Master Argon and now overrun by mutated cave rats and a band of goblin scavengers led by Chieftain Grothak. The only way back to the Surface is sealed behind a massive Vault Door in the entryway, which requires the legendary Crimson Tear to unlock. Vex must brave the Vermin Pits, navigate the Scavenger Encampment and Goblin Barracks, unlock Argon's secret Laboratory, help or appease Argon's lingering ghost, and finally confront Grothak in the Inner Sanctum to claim the Crimson Tear and win her freedom.",
    "rules": "Explore scenes, inspect readable logs for puzzle clues, unlock containers, combine alchemical ingredients to craft potent gear, and manage HP, Mana, and Stamina in turn-based combat. For the Iron-Bound Scavenger Chest, the Goblin Ledger's promise of safe access refers to reading its full safe-handling instructions, not merely knowing code 2145. Before interacting with the chest, read the ledger or carry the Picklock Set to avoid its needle trap; learning the combination from Snikt alone is not enough.",
    "intro_text": "Dust motes drift lazily through a single shaft of pale light high above—the collapsed ceiling through which you fell. You groan and push yourself up from the cold flagstones of the Dusty Entryway. Above, the rubble has completely sealed the shaft; there is no climbing back out the way you came.\n\nBefore you rises the towering silhouette of an ancient, rune-etched Vault Door, its central socket conspicuously empty where a heart-shaped gemstone should rest. To the south, a jagged archway leads deeper into the subterranean complex known in tavern whispers as the Alchemist's Folly. Faint chittering echoes from the damp dark below, mingling with the acrid tang of spilled reagents.",
    "completed_condition": "",
    "gameover_condition": "",
    "completed_guard_expression": "tw.scene.id == 'SURFACE' and tw.player.has_item('CRIMSON_TEAR')",
    "gameover_guard_expression": "tw.player.hp <= 0",
